        <h2>Privacy Policy</h2>
        <p><i>Last Updated: 7/4/2026</i></p>

        <p>By inviting OnlyOneMessage or using its functionality, you agree to this Privacy Policy.
        As mentioned in our Terms of Service, this policy may be updated at any time, including additions, removals, or edits to how data is handled.</p>

        <p><i><strong>Note:</strong> This policy applies exclusively to the hosted instance of OnlyOneMessage maintained by As2Bax.
        Self-hosted instances are operated independently and are responsible for their own data handling practices.</i></p>


        <h3>1. Information We Collect</h3>
        <p>To ensure OnlyOneMessage functions properly, we collect and store the following data:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><b>Server ID</b> - Used to identify and associate configurations with your server.</li>
            <li><b>Configured Channels</b> - Used to detect and process messages in configured channels.</li>
            <li><b>Member IDs</b> - Used for slowmode functionality. Stored temporaily for up to one month. Permanent slowmodes do not store this information.</li>
            <li><b>Configurations</b> - Settings applied via the <code>/config</code> and <code>/configchannel</code> commands.</li>
            <li><b>Usage Telemetry</b> - Anonymous data about feature usage, used only for performance insights and improvement.</li>
        </ul>


        <h3>2. How We Use Your Information</h3>
        <p>The information collected is used exclusively to operate and improve OnlyOneMessage.
        We do not sell, rent, or share any data with third parties for advertising or marketing purposes.
        All data handling is limited to what is necessary for the bot's functionality.</p>


        <h3>3. Data Retention</h3>
        <p>We retain collected data only as long as needed for the bot to operate.
        Temporary data, such as Member IDs, is automatically deleted after a maximum of 1 month.
        Usage telemetry is anonymised and discarded once the bot session ends.</p>


        <h3>4. Data Security</h3>
        <p>All data collected by the hosted instance of OnlyOneMessage is securely stored in <i>MongoDB</i>, a trusted and industry-standard database system.
        Access to this data is restricted to the developer responsible for maintaining the bot.
        Although the stored data is non-sensitive, we still take reasonable measures to prevent unauthorized access or data loss.
        No method of storage or transfer is entirely risk-free, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.</p>


        <h3>5. Self-Hosted Instances</h3>
        <p>OnlyOneMessage is open source and may be self-hosted under the
        <a href="https://github.com/As2Bax/OnlyOneMessage/blob/main/LICENSE.txt" target="_blank">AGPL-3.0 license</a>.

        As2Bax has no visibility into, or responsibility for, any data collected by self-hosted instances.
        If you are using a self-hosted instance, please contact that instance's operator regarding their data practices.</p>


        <h3>6. Your Rights & Data Removal</h3>
        <p>You may request access to, correction of, or deletion of your data at any time.
        To remove all data associated with your server, simply remove OnlyOneMessage from your server. This will immediately activate an automated deletion of all associated data.
        If you need additional help, please email <a href="mailto:me@as2bax.dev">me@as2bax.dev</a> or join our <a href="/support">Support Server</a> and create a ticket.</p>


        <h3>7. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h3>
        <p>This Privacy Policy may be updated occasionally to reflect new features or legal requirements.
        When updates occur, they will be announced in our Support Server under <strong>#announcements</strong> and on the
        <a href="https://github.com/As2Bax/OnlyOneMessage/releases" target="_blank">GitHub releases page</a>.
        
        The "Last Updated" date at the top of this page will also be updated accordingly.
        We encourage users to review this page periodically to stay informed about our data practices.</p>
